'''II.''' ''n.'' '''1.''' The science of architecture. Also ''architectonics.''—'''2.''' In ''logic'', the art of constructing systems.
{{smaller block|By ''architectonic'' I understand the art of constructing systems. ''Kant'', Critique of Pure Reason (tr. by Max Müller).}}
{{smaller block|Of these two sciences, . . . that which treats of those conditions of knowledge which lie in the nature, not of thought itself, but of that which we think about, . . . has been called . . . ''architectonic'', in so far as it treats of the method of building up our observations into system.
{{right|''Sir W. Hamilton'', Logic, App. No. I. (1866), II. 230.}}}}

